[
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_ENTER",
    "dynamic_line": "*The old smith rests his hammer against the anvil and looks up from the metal.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "text": "May we talk?",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO"
      },
      {
        "text": "I will come back later.",
        "topic": "TALK_DONE"
      }
    ],
    "speaker_effect": {
      "effect": {
        "run_eocs": "EOC_BERSERK_GODO_BEGIN"
      }
    }
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO",
    "dynamic_line": "If you came for a miracle, you've taken the wrong road. If you need honest iron, tell me what it has to do.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "text": "Who can build a prosthetic for my hand?",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_RICKERT"
      },
      {
        "text": "Can you forge a weapon for fighting demons?",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_SWORD"
      },
      {
        "text": "Can you repair what I already have?",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_REPAIR"
      },
      {
        "text": "Why do you keep forging?",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_SPARKS"
      },
      {
        "text": "May I rest here? And who is Rickert?",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_HOME"
      },
      {
        "text": "I will leave you to your work.",
        "topic": "TALK_DONE"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_SPARKS",
    "dynamic_line": "For years I thought about nothing but the next piece of iron. Heat it, strike it, watch the sparks die. Then I began to notice how much those brief lights resemble a life: bright for a moment, gone before your hand can catch them. I still forge. It's the work I know how to give to the living.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "text": "Does a weapon give a life meaning?",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_PRICE"
      },
      {
        "text": "Were you always a smith?",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_LIFE"
      },
      {
        "text": "Ask something else.",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_PRICE",
    "dynamic_line": "A blade doesn't decide why you live. Keep swinging only to fill the silence, and you'll lose whatever waited beyond the battle. I can make the iron endure. The reason to come home is your own work.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "text": "Then make something I can return with.",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_SWORD"
      },
      {
        "text": "Ask something else.",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_LIFE",
    "dynamic_line": "I've served men who wanted a beautiful blade and men who wanted an impossible one. Iron is more honest than either. Out here Rickert and I can make something useful without a lord counting every blow of the hammer.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "text": "Tell me more about the sparks.",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_SPARKS"
      },
      {
        "text": "Ask something else.",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_HOME",
    "dynamic_line": "The forge is downstairs; sleep upstairs if you need to. Keep the stair and doors clear. Rickert helps with the small moving parts and straps. We can offer a roof and a quiet corner, but walls alone will not silence that mark.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "text": "Can Rickert help me fit the cannon?",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_FITTING"
      },
      {
        "text": "Ask something else.",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_FITTING",
    "dynamic_line": "He will show you the fastenings. Once you have the finished cannon and the mount on your missing left hand, activate the cannon in your inventory. You do not have to wield it, use electricity or seek a surgeon.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "text": "What if I want to make it myself?",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_SELF"
      },
      {
        "text": "Ask something else.",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_SELF",
    "dynamic_line": "Making the cannon yourself requires fabrication 8, mechanics 4 and proper tools. Rickert can build it from your materials if you have not learned that craft. You can install the finished mechanism yourself.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "text": "Ask something else.",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO"
      }
    ]
  },
