  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BERSERK_RICKERT_GODO",
    "dynamic_line": "He says little until the iron is ready. Then one bad joint can earn more words than a whole day at the fire. Listen when he talks about coming home. The things we make are for people who still have somewhere to return.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "text": "Ask something else.",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_RICKERT"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BERSERK_RICKERT_HOME",
    "dynamic_line": "The stair leads to the sleeping loft. The forge and working tools stay below. Do not pile supplies across the stair, and keep a way to the door if your Brand wakes you at night.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "text": "Ask something else.",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_RICKERT"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_RICKERT",
    "dynamic_line": "Speak with Rickert. He builds the moving joints, grip and hidden cannon himself. I forge blades. If you already paid me for the prosthetic, your materials are still in the workshop; he will finish that same order.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "text": "Ask something else.",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BERSERK_RICKERT_PRAISE",
    "dynamic_line": {
      "u_has_bionics": "bio_berserk_hand_stump",
      "yes": "You assembled this with one hand? Those joints are not easy to fit with two. That is good work. Let us keep it working instead of making another.",
      "no": "You built the mechanism yourself? Good work. The joints tell me more than a boast would. Show it to me if it ever starts catching."
    },
    "responses": [
      {
        "text": "Return to the arm cannon order.",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_ARM"
      },
      {
        "text": "Ask something else.",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_RICKERT"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "type": "talk_topic",
    "id": "TALK_BERSERK_RICKERT_CRAFT",
    "dynamic_line": "A blade needs strength; a mechanism needs each small part to fit the next. Godot taught me to respect the metal. I work on hinges, locks and the cannon hidden in the prosthesis. In a fight I prefer a small crossbow and a clear shot. I am useful at your side, but I am not an apostle-killer with a magic sword.",
    "responses": [
      {
        "text": "Can you build my prosthesis?",
        "topic": "TALK_BERSERK_GODO_ARM"
      },
